[{:db/id "q-125738/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "4156b875-2ee5-5782-a700-8cc2fc200c44" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125738/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "943d5f3e-045d-5c4a-a441-e300aff6c89d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125738/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "ed3a1db8-5f36-588a-9cfa-34ba2c2144d7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125738/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "27fc9a35-f421-57b5-bdef-edabc4282bda" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125738/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "fd1c46e1-5f64-507b-9350-97dbc6e647e0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125738/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eebfc9ac-8103-5a63-9e56-25bf3f68b374" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125738/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-125738/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-125738/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-125738/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-125738/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-125738/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125738" :question/id #uuid "1b95d172-b59b-523e-976b-b07dae77fe4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-125738" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨2x{y}^{2},\\,2y{x}^{2}⟩$ and the points $A(1,1)$ and $B(2,8)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $F$ is conservative.\n- ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=255,$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB},$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$\n- ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=255,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the curve $y={x}^{3},$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nWith that in mind, we consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=4xy.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives exist and are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $F$ is conservative.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $F$ is conservative, there exists a function $f$ such that $∇f=F.$ Reconstructing the function $f$ from its gradient in the usual way, we get\n\n$$\nf={x}^{2}{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nApplying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =f(2,8)-f(1,1) \\\\  & ={2}^{2}\\cdot {8}^{2}-{1}^{2}\\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 64-1 \\\\  & =255.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $F$ is conservative and ${C}_{2}$ has the same initial and terminal points as ${C}_{1},$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=255.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-125738/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "72015667-33a9-53e2-a0c4-09d8ce916b54"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125738"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125748/selection/6bc991249a374b862f397b8c857af2e7218904b9402c1810129647c55070a69d" :answer/id #uuid "dd64bdb8-9011-5f9e-bf89-276616b95938" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125748/selection/0d474ca756c76f6ecddcd5fcfb411f0292ef0ce725af778ee27af0d5dc8595bc" :answer/id #uuid "b6adea54-aa77-5b1a-a6f4-4a072c08d1ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125748/selection/72443840a1994ef4e387277621cd8f464de0132f9c0b12ec6eac8b3cee6eca7d" :answer/id #uuid "02e4f1de-37de-51eb-8142-0bd8f0b378d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2e-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125748/selection/74b9878323186062e434675fc3ee407e9e4a746d2cc85ca785d4664ca99bda01" :answer/id #uuid "22af4294-2f71-50b2-8e9d-ea06db758751" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125748/selection/a2301b8122c312044fb5dc0b0c60c599b4f2f7f4ffcc198c9893873ab9165c9d" :answer/id #uuid "976ea5fd-a6fc-56bc-ab05-0521cca344b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125748/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "26bfedf0-80d8-52d7-b46b-38f5bc532188" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125748/selection/74b9878323186062e434675fc3ee407e9e4a746d2cc85ca785d4664ca99bda01" :answer-field/choices ["q-125748/selection/6bc991249a374b862f397b8c857af2e7218904b9402c1810129647c55070a69d" "q-125748/selection/0d474ca756c76f6ecddcd5fcfb411f0292ef0ce725af778ee27af0d5dc8595bc" "q-125748/selection/72443840a1994ef4e387277621cd8f464de0132f9c0b12ec6eac8b3cee6eca7d" "q-125748/selection/74b9878323186062e434675fc3ee407e9e4a746d2cc85ca785d4664ca99bda01" "q-125748/selection/a2301b8122c312044fb5dc0b0c60c599b4f2f7f4ffcc198c9893873ab9165c9d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125748" :question/id #uuid "05bb44c7-2ebe-5576-9f7a-aeb5434322c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-125748" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=2xy{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\,i+{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\,j.$ Calculate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is any smooth path from $(-1,1)$ to $(1,-1)$ in ${R}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nIn our case, the coordinates of the endpoints of the path $C$ are $A(-1,1)$ and $B(1,-1).$\n\nNotice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2x{e}^{{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives exist and are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $F$ is conservative. Therefore, we know there exists a function $f$ such that $∇f=F.$\n\nReconstructing $f$ from its gradient in the usual way, we get\n\n$$\nf=y{e}^{{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =f(1,-1)-f(-1,1) \\\\  & =(-1){e}^{{1}^{2}}-(1){e}^{(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =-e-e \\\\  & =-2e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-125748/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28bf8f3a-e97e-5ec1-bb18-3ebfa213aa46"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125748"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125749/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "99e0149f-7f4b-524c-b556-428fb6bea2ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125749/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "87c5cf42-f65d-5060-9eee-2e574cc60f9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125749/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "21f3bc07-dfd8-5488-9c29-6b67652dc8d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125749/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "6603715a-07d7-5c69-8913-b30ef4b970a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125749/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "6382c6f3-d691-5601-9882-b2e8206bb44f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125749/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c6bb2059-5f00-5757-9c17-182034afb659" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125749/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-125749/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-125749/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-125749/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-125749/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-125749/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125749" :question/id #uuid "c3254d65-fdd6-5da7-ad6c-c9b9dbeb3672" :question/math-academy-id "q-125749" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,j.$ Calculate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is any smooth path from $(-2,0)$ to $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ in ${R}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nIn our case, the coordinates of the endpoints of the path $C$ are $A(-2,0)$ and $B(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nNotice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives exist and are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $F$ is conservative. Therefore, we know there exists a function $f$ such that $∇f=F.$\n\nReconstructing $f$ from its gradient in the usual way, we get\n\n$$\nf=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =f(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})-f(-2,0) \\\\  & =1\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-125749/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28bf8f3a-e97e-5ec1-bb18-3ebfa213aa46"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125749"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125753/selection/2372eaf10d3e3c6104c5a2d85d5b9909ce1a56c36600fa4c17241dbcaf0762b2" :answer/id #uuid "d3b9545a-7689-5500-b189-5f55f53ddafd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{e}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125753/selection/4fcb670a531f37bd4190ac8b9f3fa0e7872f0044f9d3a190f33c051314d4fbcd" :answer/id #uuid "5a06e0cb-5ea1-51ea-b3b9-0382a9850e40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{2}-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125753/selection/99be353997b3ae8daee1a55922806b31687c556e62c9cfd57add7ce0ca959a98" :answer/id #uuid "8b4248bd-9525-5c22-9096-d49e0c4836e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4e-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125753/selection/6bc991249a374b862f397b8c857af2e7218904b9402c1810129647c55070a69d" :answer/id #uuid "c30ab48d-2bdb-5d2e-a4c9-24f673de4eba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125753/selection/7b1a89f374b731f00bd47d8ffad5ff5e5e58e174cfddcd2daa5a16890476b82b" :answer/id #uuid "8a0fd7a0-f4ca-5b49-a5e0-f1141004d3d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5e-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125753/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a335389-411c-57e5-8dee-5053a6d6d56b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125753/selection/99be353997b3ae8daee1a55922806b31687c556e62c9cfd57add7ce0ca959a98" :answer-field/choices ["q-125753/selection/2372eaf10d3e3c6104c5a2d85d5b9909ce1a56c36600fa4c17241dbcaf0762b2" "q-125753/selection/4fcb670a531f37bd4190ac8b9f3fa0e7872f0044f9d3a190f33c051314d4fbcd" "q-125753/selection/99be353997b3ae8daee1a55922806b31687c556e62c9cfd57add7ce0ca959a98" "q-125753/selection/6bc991249a374b862f397b8c857af2e7218904b9402c1810129647c55070a69d" "q-125753/selection/7b1a89f374b731f00bd47d8ffad5ff5e5e58e174cfddcd2daa5a16890476b82b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125753" :question/id #uuid "d893697a-cdfd-56bf-897a-d2275abdbe72" :question/math-academy-id "q-125753" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=2x{e}^{y}\\,i+{x}^{2}{e}^{y}\\,j.$ Calculate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is any smooth path from $(-1,0)$ to $(2,1)$ in ${R}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nIn our case, the coordinates of the endpoints of the path $C$ are $A(-1,0)$ and $B(2,1).$\n\nNotice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2x{e}^{y}.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives exist and are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $F$ is conservative. Therefore, we know there exists a function $f$ such that $∇f=F.$\n\nReconstructing $f$ from its gradient in the usual way, we get\n\n$$\nf={x}^{2}{e}^{y}.\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =f(2,1)-f(-1,0) \\\\  & =({2}^{2}){e}^{1}-(-1)^{2}{e}^{0} \\\\  & =4e-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-125753/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28bf8f3a-e97e-5ec1-bb18-3ebfa213aa46"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125753"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125793/selection/6f916d391661973b3a5a5637f8b1a58ee0365885b48c933d7fb44b8e52c8db65" :answer/id #uuid "b25bde75-2127-516a-ba9c-c4f2481e44a8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II, III, and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125793/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "4eb4e981-1d16-5904-98d4-8ecf16fa6105" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125793/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "06b598ac-2388-53f3-b916-ac5c5eb83af7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125793/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "9d531fa1-f63c-52ea-abe6-2d52ebebc6be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125793/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "da5f6145-d8d9-5bca-be55-3a5d56ae41cf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125793/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "11dfa3dd-5aad-5aed-bcca-cf232dee9173" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125793/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-125793/selection/6f916d391661973b3a5a5637f8b1a58ee0365885b48c933d7fb44b8e52c8db65" "q-125793/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-125793/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-125793/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-125793/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125793" :question/id #uuid "382b5216-f207-5094-bf02-ff591cd79a94" :question/math-academy-id "q-125793" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨{y}^{2},\\,-x⟩$ and the points $O(0,0)$ and $A(4,2)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=\\frac{5}{6},$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the line segment $\\overset{―}{OA},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$\n- ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=\\frac{16}{3},$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the curve $y=\\sqrt{x},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is independent of path.\n- $F$ is conservative." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nWith that in mind, we consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Parameterizing the line segment, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{1}(t)=⟨4t,\\,2t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}⟨4{t}^{2},\\,-4t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,\\,2⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}16{t}^{2}-8t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{t}^{2}-t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8{[\\frac{2{t}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =8[\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Parameterizing the curve, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{2}(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,2].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨{t}^{2},\\,-{t}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨2t,\\,1⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{{t}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3})-0 \\\\  & =8-\\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ have the same initial and terminal points, yet\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,\n$$\n\nwe conclude that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is path-dependent.\n\n- Statement IV is false. If a vector field is conservative then it is path-independent. Since $F$ is path-dependent, it is not conservative." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-125793/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "72015667-33a9-53e2-a0c4-09d8ce916b54"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125793"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
